# iio-sensor-proxy refuses to publish a proximity sensor at all without this
# property -- it logs "Found proximity sensor but no PROXIMITY_NEAR_LEVEL udev
# property" and reports HasProximity=false. Phosh needs it to blank the screen
# during a call.
#
# The driver reports 0 when clear and the sensor range (3277, i.e. 0.05 m at
# the channel's scale) when something is within range, and iio-sensor-proxy
# calls it "near" when the raw value is >= this level. Half the range is the
# threshold.
#
# Matched on ATTR{name}, not iio:deviceN: IIO device numbering depends on the
# order the SSC sensors register and is not a stable identifier.
SUBSYSTEM=="iio", ATTR{name}=="qcom-smgr-prox-light", ENV{PROXIMITY_NEAR_LEVEL}="1638"
